    "ssrd_evening_segment: CDS hourly ssrd accumulations decline (not grow) over ~19-23 UTC daily in every month sampled (Jan+Jul 2020 verified), which is impossible for same-origin accumulations (production-stream mixing). Clipped de-accumulation therefore yields ~0 W/m2 for those hours and the observed diurnal peaks ~15 UTC vs true solar noon ~17:20 UTC at footprint mean lon: the SHAPE is distorted, not just the evenings. solar_radiation_wm2 is valid for day/night contrast and rough magnitude (deep-night ~0 verified; midday mean >30 W/m2) but NOT for precise intraday solar timing. daylight_proxy (timestamp-derived, unaffected) + cloud_cover carry the unbiased diurnal shape. Follow-up: re-pull ssrd via an alternative CDS stream/format or derive evening solar from clear-sky x cloud.",
